  {
    "episode_id": 66265,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/6/6/66265.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 16,
    "turn_text": "Sarah Jane was a nurse, a civilian nurse, and my buddy Jane and I were working at the Naval Hospital in San Diego, California. We ran into each other, started talking, I invited to my graduation from hospital core school. That's a medic for people that aren't familiar with Navy terms. And she came to my graduation when we started dating. Our first date was to First Presbyterian Church in downtown San Diego, which was kind of a thing for me. I had no religious affiliation at that point. I was raised in Amal, really a cultural Catholic. I came to Christ, actually, through my wife, interestingly enough. We got married, and when we were having our second child, we sat down and talked about this and realized how incredibly important faith is. I saw it in her. It's kind of a strange thing, and I realized she was the person that I trusted more than any other human being on the earth, and if this was so important to her that I need to look at it. And that's when I started my walk with faith. That was back in 1993. And you have children, how many children do you have? We have four children and six grandchildren. It's two girls and two boys. The girls, ones in Virginia, ones here with us in Prairie. And then one of our boys is in the service right now. And then the youngest one just got engaged yesterday. He is starting his master's degree in biblical ex-Jesus coming up here in the fall.",
