    "turn_idx": 19,
    "turn_text": "you. I look back. So when I turned 18 years old, this is how much of a goofball was. I dropped out of high school when I was 16 years old. I thought I knew everything just like every other 16 year old does. I've been supporting myself since then. I joined the Navy in 18, got a GED. I didn't get an undergraduate degree until I was 44 years old. It's wonderful how your family grows, your faith grows, your understanding the world grows, and the longer you've been in this moral coil, the more you really understand how things work and what a positive effect you can have if you really apply yourself. I see that more and more every day.",
